# SVG Logo Source

When adding or replacing brand, product, or technology logos as SVG, get them from **[svglogos.dev](https://svglogos.dev/)** only.

## Default

- Search and download logos from https://svglogos.dev/
- Prefer official SVG assets from that library over other CDNs, Simple Icons, Wikipedia, or random web scrapes
- Save into the project's existing logo folders (`src/assets/tech/`, `src/assets/logos/`) using clear kebab-case filenames

## Exceptions

Use a different source only when the user **explicitly** says so, or when:

- The logo is custom/proprietary and not on svglogos.dev (e.g. personal brand, client mark)
- The user provides a file or URL to use instead
- A non-SVG format is required (PNG/WebP) and no suitable SVG exists on svglogos.dev — ask before substituting

## Examples

```text
❌ BAD: Pull React/n8n/GitHub logos from random Google/CDN results
✅ GOOD: Download the SVG from svglogos.dev, then add it under src/assets/

❌ BAD: Invent or redraw a brand mark when svglogos.dev has it
✅ GOOD: Use the svglogos.dev asset; note if the mark is missing and ask
```
